/// \defgroup grp_w3_ini_field_callbacks Field lookup, flag names and small field parsers
/// \ingroup grp_ini
/// \brief How a field name finds its parser, how flag and science names
///        become numbers, and a set of small field parsers for global,
///        object, audio, particle and horde data.
///
/// When the INI reader fills a block, INI::initFromINIMulti reads each
/// line's first token as the field name and asks findFieldParse for the
/// parse function that handles it. The parse function then reads the rest
/// of the line. This group documents that lookup, the name-to-number
/// lookups many parsers rely on (BitFlags::getSingleBitFromName for flag
/// sets, INI::scanScience for sciences), ParseAlphaNumericBitMask (a
/// one-letter-per-bit notation; no call or pointer to it has been found in
/// the retail executable), and a number of small, mostly file-local field
/// parsers. The INI class page explains the field parser signature they
/// share; \ref sub_ini is the subsystem page for the load as a whole.
///
/// \par INI keys handled here
/// The keys below were read from the FieldParse rows in the retail
/// executable that point at each parser. The syntax shown uses colons;
/// wherever a parser reads with the colon separator set, a space, a tab or
/// an equals sign works as well.
/// - GeometryRotationAnchorOffset, ClearanceGeometryRotationAnchorOffset:
///   X:x Y:y (parseGeometryRotationAnchorOffset).
/// - MultiPlayUnitXPMult, MultiPlayBuildingXPMult, MultiPlayUnitSpeedMult,
///   MultiPlayBuildingSpeedMult: pairs such as MP1:1.0 MP2:1.25
///   (parseMultiPlayUnitXPMult and its siblings).
/// - Human, Computer, LoadAIScripts: Yes or No; ForcePlayerTeam: an integer
///   (parseHuman, parseComputer, parseLoadAIScripts, parseForcePlayerTeam).
/// - ReallyLowMHz, AudioLowMHz: top-level keywords taking an integer
///   (parseReallyLowMHz, parseAudioLowMHz).
/// - Delay: two integers; PitchShift, PerFilePitchShift: two reals
///   (parseDelay, parsePitchShift).
/// - Color1 to Color8: R:r G:g B:b frame; Alpha1 to Alpha8: low high frame
///   (ParticleSystemTemplate::parseRGBColorKeyframe,
///   ParticleSystemTemplate::parseRandomKeyframe).
/// - TargetTypes: a list of AI kind names (parseAIKindOfList).
/// - BannerCarrierPosition: UnitType:name Pos:X:x Y:y;
///   SplitHorde: SplitResult:name UnitType:name, optionally RankNumber:n
///   (parseBannerCarrierPosition, parseHordeContainSplitResult).
///
/// \par Modding
/// - Field names are matched exactly, including case (findFieldParse).
///   Flag names looked up through BitFlags::getSingleBitFromName are
///   matched without regard to case, and so are the MPn slot names of the
///   multiplier keys. The sub-keywords of the horde parsers (UnitType, Pos,
///   SplitResult, RankNumber) are case-sensitive.
/// - The flag-name and AI-kind tables in this group are compiled into the
///   executable; data can use their entries but cannot add new ones.
///   (Sciences are the exception: INI::scanScience looks them up among the
///   sciences that Science.ini defines.)

